    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1eeddbd4_6dbc4eb8",
        "filename": "libs/binder/rust/src/proxy.rs",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 723,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944400
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-27T22:51:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "i think you can cut down on some of the unsafe (e.g. in the drop impl and the explicit `cookie_incr_refcount` in `new`) if you do something like this\n\n```\npub struct Accessor\u003cF: Fn() -\u003e Option\u003cConnectionInfo\u003e + Send + Sync + \u0027static\u003e {\n    accessor: *mut sys::ARpc_Accessor,\n    callback: Arc\u003cF\u003e,\n}\n```\n\nif we don\u0027t want to make `Accessor` generic, you could do something like `callback: Box\u003cdyn Drop\u003e` to erase the type (needs an extra alloc though) or use `Arc\u003cdyn Fn() -\u003e Option\u003cConnectionInfo\u003e + Send + Sync + \u0027static\u003e` throughout (which is basically the rust equiv of `std::function\u003c...\u003e`)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 719,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 723,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "0f6344943c3be2bf3055943f85d83e5fc65a8a68",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0c293ce2_7ac00efe",
        "filename": "libs/binder/rust/src/proxy.rs",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 723,
      "author": {
        "id": 1644679
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-30T22:01:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we need the extra `increase_strong_count` to keep the object alive until the NDK API calls the `cookie_decr_refcount`. (passing ownership when passing the function pointer + the object pointer to the NDK API).\n\nI think we don\u0027t need this Accessor object to hold a reference to it at all. Removing that cleaned up a lot!\n\nDoes this make sense? Is there another more rusty way to pass ownership of this object to libbinder_ndk?",
      "parentUuid": "1eeddbd4_6dbc4eb8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 719,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 723,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "0f6344943c3be2bf3055943f85d83e5fc65a8a68",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "db121639_c09e371e",
        "filename": "libs/binder/rust/src/proxy.rs",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 723,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944400
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-03T22:46:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think that makes sense. `DeathRecipient` wants to keep a ref count on the cookie itself, but there seems to be no need here, so you can let the NDK hold the only reference.\n\nI think what you\u0027ve done is a bit wrong though. When you do `Arc::new`, the ref count is at 1. Then `Arc::increment_strong_count` increases the count to 2. When you call `ARpc_Accessor_delete`, I expect it to call `cookie_decr_refcount` exactly one time, which brings the count down to 1. Then, nothing else does a decr, so it looks like a leak.\n\n(`Arc::into_raw` takes ownership of the existing ref count represented by the `Arc` value consumed. it doesn\u0027t do any decr or incr)",
      "parentUuid": "0c293ce2_7ac00efe",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 719,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 723,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "0f6344943c3be2bf3055943f85d83e5fc65a8a68",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
